  "result": "I fixed the paging bug in `src/server/repositories/_paging.ts`. I haven't run the tests or walked any list page by page to confirm it.\n\n**Cause:** the \"next page\" filter only asked for rows with a timestamp older than the last row shown. Entries recorded at the same moment as that last row were therefore dropped. That is why bulk imports, notification bursts and bulk audit-log changes lost entries, while gradually created lists paged fine.\n\n**Fix:** the filter now also keeps rows that share the last row's timestamp but have a smaller id. This matches the existing sort order (newest first, then id descending), so every row should appear exactly once, in the same order as one large page.\n\nThe same helper drives the issue, notification, audit-log, comment, project, member and search lists, so all of them get the fix. Each of those queries still applies its own workspace filter alongside the paging filter, so other workspaces' entries stay excluded.",
